title: Why recently viewed is kept by the GUI
tags: [[Panel types]]
kind: rationale
audience: dev
summary: The list of metarecords last looked at is a file of the GUI, not a field of the metarecord: a view must not be a write; it stores a time and a rank, and the panel shows a snapshot.

!! A view is not a write

The obvious place for "last viewed" is a field on the metarecord. But every write to
the daemon goes through the event log: one write, and a new version of the
metarecord, per write ([[Writes and atomicity]]). Recording each ''view'' that way
would fill the history with writes nobody made, put them in the way of
<<key "log:undo" Ctrl+z>>, and change a version that other clients compare.

So the list is the GUI's, as the input history is ([[Input history]]): one text file
per repository, `.metafolder/gui/recent`, a line `<uuid>` tab `<ISO-8601 time>` tab
`<rank>` per metarecord, newest first. Viewing a metarecord again moves its line to
the front rather than adding one. `crates/gui/src/recent.rs` holds it, behind
`metafolder.recent.touch` and `metafolder.recent.list` ([[The metafolder API]]); the
[[metarecord-detail panel]] and the [[file panel]] call `touch` when the metarecord they
show changes, and not when the same one is reloaded; the [[file-manager panel]] when it
goes into another folder.

!! A time and a rank

Each line carries when the metarecord was last viewed and a ''rank'': one per view,
aged as zoxide ages its own, so that [[Frecent folders]] can tell a folder used every
day from one opened once. The rank is per line and not a position in a global order:
with a time and a rank on each line, the file ''is'' the state, nothing has to be read
back at start, and the panel can say "3 min ago" for free. A line of the older
two-column form, from before the rank, reads as one view.

What the rank is worth is not decided here: `recent.rs` only counts and ages, and
the weighting by recency — the ''score'' the panel and the picks show — is `frecency`
in the shared panel helpers ([[Frecent folders]]). The rank itself is not shown: the
score is what orders, so it is the one number on screen.

!! The panel shows a snapshot

The [[recent panel]] reads the list when it is shown, on a refresh and when
metarecords change — not at each view. Moving its cursor selects a row, which the
detail panel beside it shows, which is a view: a live list would reorder itself under
the cursor at every step.

!! The pick does not need the panel

`recent`, the pick of the command input, is defined in the shipped `gui/commands.js`
([[User commands]]) and reads the same list: it works whether or not the panel was
ever shown, and its lines are reshaped there (`recentLine`).
